  "body": "Paired AMD MI350X numerical evidence for the independently adapted FlashInfer RMSNorm at width16384, native block1024/wave64, and rows1,3,64,255.\n\nEach host completed 24 paired trials (48 launches). All 127,008,768 CPU float64 comparisons pass at atol=rtol=0.002, with separate Torch FP32 checks, read-only inputs and allocation guards. Each method matches across hosts. Per-host adapted/upstream differences remain explicit: 3,422,543 signed-zero differences and 264 other one-ULP differences.\n\nThe four assets retain every input, both complete output streams on both hosts, compiler captures, standalone audit sources, nine rehashed numerical rejection controls, and the source/address component proof packets. The selected upstream template body is retained verbatim with disclosed HIP helper substitutions. All thirteen component/regression CI jobs pass at the recorded source revision.\n\nComplete native source execution and dense-real correctness proofs remain pending. Registered FlashInfer source certificates: zero. Original paper model/token-cost results and NVIDIA measurements remain unreproduced.\n"
